The Fee formula uses a conditional expression. Changing the input never changes its definition: elapsed time and billable fees remain linked to the recorded session.

# Review
**Acme Manufacturing | a connected model at a glance**

These results are calculated from the other five sheets. They are not pasted summaries. Named references keep the relationship readable, while filter and lookup answer questions about the ledgers.

**Try it:** open Sales Ledger and change invoice ACME-003. Return here to see the lookup result change. Then change an input in Start Here and compare the plan and financing results.

| @meta |  || {:,.2f} |
|  | Measure || Value |
|  | --- || --- |
|  | 2026 planned revenue || = @["Operating Report"::["Total revenue","2026.H1"]] + @["Operating Report"::["Total revenue","2026.H2"]] |
|  | 2027 planned revenue || = @["Operating Report"::["Total revenue","2027.H1"]] + @["Operating Report"::["Total revenue","2027.H2"]] |
|  | 2026 net income || = @["Operating Report"::["Net income","2026.H1"]] + @["Operating Report"::["Net income","2026.H2"]] |
|  | Net invoice sales || = sum(@["Sales Ledger"::F2:F25]) |
|  | Open invoice value || = sum(filter(@["Sales Ledger"::H2:H25], @["Sales Ledger"::I2:I25] == "Open")) |
|  | Paid invoice value || = sum(filter(@["Sales Ledger"::H2:H25], @["Sales Ledger"::I2:I25] == "Paid")) |
|  | Invoice ACME-003 || = lookup("ACME-003", @["Sales Ledger"::A2:A25], @["Sales Ledger"::H2:H25]) |
|  | First-year loan payments || = sum(@["Loan Planner"::C2:C13]) |
|  | First-year loan interest || = -cumipmt(@["Start Here"::["Loan annual rate","Value"]] / 12, @["Start Here"::["Loan years","Value"]] * 12, @["Start Here"::["Loan principal","Value"]], 1, 12, 0) |
|  | First-year principal repaid || = -cumprinc(@["Start Here"::["Loan annual rate","Value"]] / 12, @["Start Here"::["Loan years","Value"]] * 12, @["Start Here"::["Loan principal","Value"]], 1, 12, 0) |
| {:.1f} | Delivery hours || = sum(@["Delivery Sessions"::F2:F17]) |
| {:.1f} | Billable delivery hours || = sum(filter(@["Delivery Sessions"::F2:F17], @["Delivery Sessions"::G2:G17])) |
|  | Service fees || = sum(@["Delivery Sessions"::H2:H17]) |
| {:.1%} | Revenue growth assumption || = @["Start Here"::["Revenue growth","Value"]] |
| {:.1%} | Probability below one standard deviation || = normalCdf(1) |

**Where to go next**

Use File → Examples to explore the larger company report, valuation, mortgage and operations models. You can reopen Getting started at any time from that menu.

Keep an Ordinate copy for editable notes, formulas and structure. For an Excel copy, choose Export and inspect the conversion review. Enable Freeze headers only if you want fixed row and column headers in Excel.

There is no separate tutorial mode: every note, input and formula in this workbook can be edited normally.
